          "en": "Tautologies are mere repetitions, like “x=x\" or “x is either y or not y,” or ‘whatever has legs and toes has toes.” *Rational animals are animals™is a tautology; a computer can tell that it is self-evidently true. But *all men are mortal” is not a tautology; it requires insight into thc comprehension of “man” to know that “all men are mortal” is necessarily true, and some people have that insight while others do not.\n\nComputers do not have the power of insight. We need more than computer logic because we are more than computers. There are enough logics around for computers, and not enough for humans.",
