          "en": "1. The end of a thing is its purpose and perfection, and death is the end of life, therefore death 1s life's purpose and perfection.\n\n2. Cancer is made of human cells, and whatever is made of human cells is human, and what is human should not be killed, so cancer should not be killed.\n\n3. Innuendo is an ltalian suppository.\n\n4. Condemned prisoner to judge: “But I don’t feel guilty.” 5. Condemned prisoner to judge: “You're a bad man, judge; you're terribly judgmental.” 6. Condemned prisoner to judge: “You're supposed to do justice, judge. But you've just done a bad thing. and a bad thing can’t be just, because justice is a good thing, not a bad thing.” *What bad thing have I done?” **You've lowered my self-cstcem in declaring me guilty. Self-esteem is good, and you've taken away something good. so you're bad. You should be punished instead of me.” 7. There shouldn't be laws against drugs, because the people who usc drugs don’t believe there should be laws against them, and that means the coun- try doesn’t have consensus about it, and laws should reflect the people's conscnsus.\n\n8. Philosophy is a kind of love - the love of wisdom. Therefore philosophy teachers who accept salaries are mercenary lovers. They're intellectual prostitutes; they sell their love for money.\n\n9. Antigravity should be casy. We disobey all kinds of laws, even the law of non-contradiction, so we should be able to disobey the law of gravity.",
