          "en": "Outlining is not simply putting numbers and letters in order before sen- tences or before headings. They must be in logical order and logical subordina- fion.\n\nStudents usually dislike outlining because they find it mechanical and inflexible. But when we construct any work of art with a complex structure, whether a garage or a symphony, there is simply no companson between having a plan or outlinc and not having onc.",
