          "en": "(3) Every one of the actors in this movie is great, so it must be a great movie.\n\n(4) “An arrow that appears to be in flight must really be at rest, for when a thing occupies a space equal to itself, it is at rest. Since the arrow never occu- pies a space greater or smaller than itself, it is always at rest. Since the arrowis at rest at each moment offlight, it can never move.” (Zeno the Eleatic) (Math majors should explain howthe infinitesimal calculus answers Zeno's puzzle.) (5) “There's a bug on this blade of grass.” *My goodness. you certainly have a buggy lawn.” 3D, Division This is the reverse of Composition; it consists in arguing from whole to pan, ignoring the fact that what is truc of thc whole is not always true ofthe part.\n\nIt too can be done either with single things (“That book is fascinating, there- fore cach chapter must be”) or with groups (“That class is smart, and he's a member ofit, therefore he must be smart™).\n\nExamples:\n\n(1) If ten glasses of wine per meal is harmful to health, then one glass of winc per meal must also be harmful to health, for it cannot be that many good things make one bad thing.\n\n(2) Inshmen are scattered all over the world. Pat is an Inshman. Therefore Pat 1s scattered all over the world.\n\n(3) “A frugal shepherd will buy only black sheep, not white sheep.” *1 did not know that. Why is that so?” “Because white sheep eat more than black sheep.” “I did not know that cither. Why is that so?\" “Why,it's obvious. White sheep eat more than black sheep because there are more white sheep than black sheep.”",
