          "speakerAm": "ገጽ 101 (የቀጠለ)",
          "role": "prose",
          "en": "Stercotypes are artificial, socially fabricated, and changeable.\n\nArchetypes are givens in the “collective unconscious.” “Women are weak and inferior’ is a stereotype; “the sea is a woman” is an archetype. “The Jewish mother” is a stereotype; “Mother Earth” is an archetype. G.I. Joc is a stercotype; Ares, or Mars, the god of war,is an archetype.\n\nNot all generalizations are stereotypes.\n\nIn fact, onc of the most misused stereotypes in modern discourse is that of the stereotype, for it is fashionable to call every generalization a stereotype.\n\nHere are some real examples of stereotypes:\n\n“You're tall; you must play basketball.” “You're Black; you must dance well.” “You're a man; you must throw your socks on the floor.” “You'rc a woman; you must get bad PMS.” “You're an American; you must be nch.”",
