          "speaker": "Page 117: Procedural fallacies",
          "speakerAm": "ገጽ 117፦ Procedural fallacies",
          "role": "prose",
          "en": "Procedural fallacies explanations claim less than proofs, they are less controversial, less threatening, less confrontational; so it is tempting to usc them instead of proofs. This is not a fallacy, if we know what we are doing: but it is a fallacy when we confuse the two and think that our explanation amounts to a proof.\n\nE.¢.\n\nDarwinian Natural Selection explains the fossil record, and does so more scientifically than any other hypothesis. However, Natural Selection is an explanation, not a proof. First of all, it is not put forward as a proof of the fossil record (for no onc questions that record: it is not controversial; it is not a con- clusion of an argument, but it is data). It is put forward as a hypothesis that explains the fossil record.\n\nSecond, the Darwinian argument for Natural Sclection, including the evidence of the fossil record, amounts to a probable argument, but not a “door-shutting™proof — at least so far. Copemicus’s helio- centric hypothesis too was only an explanation. not a proof, until subsequent obscrvations refuted the alternative Ptolemaic geocentnc hypothesis.\n\nSimilarly, the Freudian explanation of religion as fear-induced father-fig- urc-fantasy docs not prove religion is an illusion, any more than the religious explanation of Freud's athcism as his own Oedipus complex proves that Freud was wrong about God.\n\nOE, Answering Another Argument than the One Given Students on tests often change the question given to them from one that they cannot answer to one that they can, and then answer it. Similarly, in the middle of an argument we often hear someone come up with a brilliant refutation - of an argument that was not given. He has slain the enemy, but the wrong enemy.\n\nPerhaps he hopes that the brilliance of his refutation will distract attention away from his sidestepping the original argument.",
          "am": "ይህ ክፍል በገጽ 117 ላይ የቀረበውን የሶክራታዊ ሎጂክ ዋና ሐሳብ ያካትታል። ሙሉው የእንግሊዝኛ ይዘት በትይዩ ተቀምጧል።",
