          "en": "I.\n\nTerms Il.\n\nPropositions Ill.\n\nArguments (inferences) A. Immediate inference (only one premise, and only two terms) 1. Obversion 2. Conversion 3. Combined forms B. Mediate inference (more than one premise, and more than two terms) I.Deductive (usually syllogism) a. Simple b. Compound (1) hypothetical (2) disjunctive (3) conjunctive 2. Inductive Section 2. Conversion (B) When we “convert” a proposition, we interchange the subject and the predicate.\n\nFor instance, “No man is an island” becomes “No island 1s a man.” and “Some",
