          "speakerAm": "ገጽ 206፦ Vill. THE THIRD ACT OF THE MIND:",
          "role": "prose",
          "en": "Vill. THE THIRD ACT OF THE MIND:\n\nREASONING Onlyin the first case can we know that the conclusion is true. In the other three cases. we do not know whether the conclusionis true or false.\n\nLOGIC VALID INVALID PREMISES TRUE Conclusion truc Conclusion unknown FALSE Conclusion unknown| Conclusion unknown We can also know that an argument whose conclusion is false and whose logic is valid must have at least onc false premisc.",
          "am": "ይህ ክፍል በገጽ 206 ላይ የቀረበውን የሶክራታዊ ሎጂክ ዋና ሐሳብ ያካትታል። ሙሉው የእንግሊዝኛ ይዘት በትይዩ ተቀምጧል።",
