          "en": "9. Men pitch bascballs faster than women because they have more upper body muscle strength.\n\n10. Women’s voices are higher than men’s because their vocal cords are dif- ferent.\n\n11. The ball will land in the seats because the home run hitteris up.\n\n12. Children ask questions because the reason we're here is to knowtruth.\n\n13. The tide is high because the moon is full.\n\n14. The iron filings are moving because there's a magnet here.\n\n15. It’s water because it’s two parts hydrogen and one part oxygen.\n\n16. E.T. is a person because he can communicate.\n\nSection 3. A classification of arguments We can classify arguments by different standards:\n\n(1) By form: Arguments may be cither immediate inference (Chapter VII) or mediate inference. Immediate inference contains only onc premise and only",
