          "role": "prose",
          "en": "IX. DIFFERENT KINDS OF ARGUMENTS philosophy (e.g. the metaphysical Theory of Forms, the anthropological dualism of body and soul, and the cpistemological rationalism and theory of knowledge as “recollection” of innate ideas), agrees with and uses these five steps himsclf.\n\nIn fact, these five steps are not some specialized, esoteric method proper to Socrates alone, or the Greeks alone, but they constitute the most natural and complete movement of human knowledge.\n\nFrom the Anstotelian point of view, seven alternative theories of knowledge can be seen to exaggerate one of the steps. or to omit onc of the steps, or to wrongly order the steps. of this Socratic scheme. (1) Dogmatism (in the popular sensc) omits step one, the question, or the questionablencss of the question.",
          "am": "ይህ ክፍል በገጽ 224 ላይ የቀረበውን የሶክራታዊ ሎጂክ ዋና ሐሳብ ያካትታል። ሙሉው የእንግሊዝኛ ይዘት በትይዩ ተቀምጧል።",
