          "role": "prose",
          "en": "X. SYLLOGISMS (4) Finally. identify thc middle term as the termthat is lefi, the term that is not in the conclusion but is in cach premise.\n\nFrom now on we will use the following standard abbreviations:\n\nS = the minor term P = the major term M = the middle term We use S for the minor term because it is always the subject (S) of the con- clusion. It is not always the subject of the minor premise, however. Sometimes it is and sometimes it is not. But even when it is the predicate of the minor prem- isc. we will use the symbol S forit, since it is always the subject of the conclu- sion.\n\nWe use P for the major term because it is always the predicate (P) of the conclusion.\n\nIt is not always the predicate of the major premise, however.",
          "am": "ይህ ክፍል በገጽ 226 ላይ የቀረበውን የሶክራታዊ ሎጂክ ዋና ሐሳብ ያካትታል። ሙሉው የእንግሊዝኛ ይዘት በትይዩ ተቀምጧል።",
