          "en": "The structure and strategy ofa syllogism negative). To do this, we relate both S and P to the same common third term, M.\n\nThe middle tenn is the touchstone; we test whether or not S and P belong togeth- er by touching both to M, as we would test whether two magnets have the same polarity by touching them both to the same third magnet to sec whether they react to it in the same way or in opposite ways.\n\nImagine a bndge over a nver. The middle term 1s the middle ofthe bndge.\n\nS and P are the two ends of the bridge, where it touches the land. The major and minor premises are the two halves of the bridge: the major premise connects M (the middlec of the bndge) with P (one end of the bndge) and the minor premise connects M with S (the other end of the bndge). It is M that either holds the bridge together or makes it fall apart. The middle term is the center and key of the syllogism, the hinge on which it tums.",
          "am": "ይህ ክፍል በገጽ 227 ላይ የቀረበውን የሶክራታዊ ሎጂክ ዋና ሐሳብ ያካትታል። ሙሉው የእንግሊዝኛ ይዘት በትይዩ ተቀምጧል።",
