          "en": "8A. Capital punishment is morally right.\n\n8B. Capital punishment is not morally right.\n\n9A. All abortions are morally wrong.\n\n9B. Not all abortions arc morally wrong.\n\nD.\n\nWhenever we have two apparently good syllogisms which prove conclusions that contradict cach other. which you constructed in exercise C, we must have in ar least one of each pair of syllogisms either a term used ambigu- ously, or a false premise. or a logical fallacy. In this exercise you are to find one of these three possible weaknesses in both arguments of cach pair. You probably consider the syllogism that proves the conclusion you agree with to be the stronger one, so it is a challenging and useful exercise to try to find the weakness that your opponent will find in that ong, i.c. in your own argu- ment, as well as the weakness in his.",
