          "role": "prose",
          "en": "Therefore this candidate must be a Communist.\n\ntw insist on the abolition of private property No. he might be against private property for other reasons. He might be an anar- chist, or a spiritualist who wants to deny all maternal property because he believes matter is an illusion; or a monk who wants the whole world to live in a global monastery, or a tyrant who wants to possess all property himself.\n\nBut the form ofthis deceptive argumentis exactly the same as the form of the first onc (about cats and dogs), which is not deceptive because of its clearer content. The common form is:\n\nAllPis M Andall Sis M Thercforc all Sis P ® ®",
