          "en": "The list of names includes other devices as well. E.g. the letter *'s™after the vowels “E™or “I” indicates that when the E proposition can be converted sim- ply (*'s™), the syllogism is transformed. or “reduced” into one of the first figure, the figure which Anistotle and the medicvals regarded as the most clear, simple, natural, and direct. There arc also other details in the scheme. e.g. using the same initial consonant for syllogisms that can be “reduced” to cach other. All this claboratc logical dancing was done naturally, easily, and without reference to a text by medieval debaters.\n\nSection 4. Venn Diagrams Venn Diagrams are quite efficient in distinguishing valid and invalid syllogisms:\n\nhowever, they do not reveal the fallacy, the reason for the invalidity. Like",
