          "en": "Venn Diagrams cxistential and all universal propositions as non-cxistcntial, so that under this assumption a particular proposition can claim more than a universal. So because ofthe basic rule (common to both Anistotelian and Boolean logic) that there may not be more in the conclusion than in the premises, the Venn-Boolean system has the opposite rule from Aristotle's system: in Aristotelian logic it is fallacious to derive a universal conclusion from a particular premise; in the Venn (Boolean) system it is fallacious to denive a particular conclusion from universal premises.\n\nA particular conclusion from two universal premises is not necessanly a fal- lacy by Anistotle’s rules. Take the following syllogism:\n\nAll leprechauns are green.\n\nAll Icprechauns are clever.",
          "am": "ይህ ክፍል በገጽ 273 ላይ የቀረበውን የሶክራታዊ ሎጂክ ዋና ሐሳብ ያካትታል። ሙሉው የእንግሊዝኛ ይዘት በትይዩ ተቀምጧል።",
