          "en": "And all mammals sleep.\n\nTherefore Moby Dick sleeps.\n\nThe only difference between the first and second versions above is that the first version omits a step. viz. the conclusion of the first syllogism in the two- syllogism version: “Moby Dick is a mammal.” A sonites may be only two syllogisms together. as in the above cxample, or more than two, up to any number. E.g. “all Ais Band all Bis Cand all Cis D and all D is E and all E is F therefore all A is FE” For instance. “suffering produces endurance, and endurance produces character, and character produces hope, and hope does not disappoint us™(Romans 5:3-5). We can translate this into:\n\nAll who suffer, endure.\n\nAll who endure, develop character.\n\nAll who develop character, have hope.\n\nAll who have hope will not be disappointed.\n\nTherefore all who suffer, will not be disappointed.\n\ntw will not be disappointed twhave hope (er tw endure tw develop character ~~ The final conclusion is implied in the quotation, as in a third order enthymeme. St. Paul scemed to be attached to this kind of sorites. There is anoth- cr one in Romans 8:29-30. (Look it up. If you don’t have a Bible, steal one.)",
