          "en": "Section 1. Hypothetical syllogisms (B) There are two forms of hypothetical syllogisms (i.e. syllogisms that begin with a hypothetical (*'if .\n\n.\n\n. then. ..”) proposition: pure hypothetical syllogisms and mixed hypothetical syllogisms. The first form is fairly rare, the second form is very common.\n\nIn a pure hypothetical syllogism, all three propositions are hypothetical propositions. E.g., If it rains, I will get wet, And if I get wet, 1 will be cold.\n\nTherefore if it rains, I will be cold.",
