          "role": "prose",
          "en": "Conjunctive syllogisms In disjunctive form, it becomes:\n\nEither Socrates is not a man, or he is mortal.\n\nBut hc is a man (he is not not-a-man) Therefore he is mortal.\n\nAnd in conjunctive form, it becomes:\n\nSocrates cannot both be a man and not be monal.\n\nBut Socrates 1s a man.\n\nTherefore Socrates is not not-mortal (he is mortal).\n\nIf we begin not with a simple syllogism but with a compound one, we get the same exchange possibilities:\n\nIf it rains, we will get wet.\n\nAnd it will rain.",
          "am": "ይህ ክፍል በገጽ 315 ላይ የቀረበውን የሶክራታዊ ሎጂክ ዋና ሐሳብ ያካትታል። ሙሉው የእንግሊዝኛ ይዘት በትይዩ ተቀምጧል።",
