          "role": "prose",
          "en": "Dilemmas Exercises: Put each of the following dilemmas in symbolic form, then answer cach one.\n\n“An unhappy alternative is before you, Elizabeth. From this day you must be a stranger to one of your parents. Your mother will never see you again if you do not marry Mr. Collins, and | will never sce you again if you do.” (Jane Austen, Pride and Prejudice) . “Culture is on the horns of this dilemma: if profound and noble, it must rcmain rare; if common, it must become mean.” (George Santayana) .\n\n“Pain is unavoidable, for if we satisfy our desires we feel satiation and boredom; and if we do not, we feel restlessness and discomfort.” (Arthur Schopenhauer) . (H) “A man cannot inquire cither about that which he knows, or about that which he does not know. Forif he knows, he has no need to inquire; and if not, he cannot inquire, for he does not know the very thing about which he is to inquire.” (Plato, AMeno) . King Henry VII's tax collector collected enormous amounts of taxes from the people, arguing that “If you have been spending little, you must be rich through your savings: and if you have been spending much, you must be rich in order to spend so much.” .\n\nCaliph Omar justified buming the world’s greatest library. at Alexandna. by this dilemma: “These books either agree with the Qur*an or they do not. If they agree, they are superfluous. If they disagree, they are heretical. In either casc, they should be burned.” .",
          "am": "ይህ ክፍል በገጽ 321 ላይ የቀረበውን የሶክራታዊ ሎጂክ ዋና ሐሳብ ያካትታል። ሙሉው የእንግሊዝኛ ይዘት በትይዩ ተቀምጧል።",
          "notes": "Peter Kreeft, Socratic Logic (Ed. 3.1), Page 321."
