          "role": "prose",
          "en": "Arguments by analogy that these things will also be similar in another way. Schematically, the argument from analogy looks like this:\n\nEntities 1, 11, 111, and IV all have attnbutes A, B, and C.\n\nEnttics 1, 11, and 111 also have attnbute D.\n\nTherefore entity 1V will probably also have attnbute D.\n\nThe criteria that make an argument from analogy more probable are:\n\n(1) The number of entities observed in the premises.\n\n(2) The variety of entities observed in the premises.\n\n(3) The number ofattributes in which the entities are similar.",
          "am": "ይህ ክፍል በገጽ 341 ላይ የቀረበውን የሶክራታዊ ሎጂክ ዋና ሐሳብ ያካትታል። ሙሉው የእንግሊዝኛ ይዘት በትይዩ ተቀምጧል።",
