          "en": "But our women are happy. That proves they ‘re not oppressed.\n\nWho says they're happy?\n\nThey do! We do! And if they say they're happy. then they're happy. How could you be mistaken about that?\n\nYou can’t be as happy as American women arc. Look at all the things we have that you can’t have . .\n\nDon’t bother listing the things. Things can’t make you happy.\n\nWell, we've got the happiness and we've got the things; don't you think that shows there's a connection?\n\nYou don 1 have the happiness. You're not as happy as we are.\n\nWait a minute. You just said no onc could be mistaken about whether she’s happy or not. Now you're saying we re mistaken about being happy.\n\nNo. I'm saying you're unhappy and you knowit. The polls show it. The statistics show it. The suicides showit.\n\nAnd does Iraq have polls and statistics? Can we compare?\n\nWe can compare us, anyway. You are an American woman, arcn't you? And | am an Iraqi woman, right?\n\nYes.\n\nAnd which one of us is smiling and which one frowning now?\n\nBut...\n\nPlease answer my question, and then | will answer yours.\n\nYou're smiling and I'm frowning. But .\n\n.\n\nAnd do people smile when they're unhappy? And do they frown when they’re happy?\n\nNo. but...\n\nSee? American women are unhappy and Iraqi women are happy.\n\nWhat makes the difference? What's the missing factor in America that’s present in Iraq? Islamic law. Islamic law makes us happy.\n\nThe proof of the pudding is in the cating — isn't that what you say? And may | also tell you why you arc unhappy?\n\nWhy?\n\nBecause you are oppressed.\n\nWhat? He re oppressed?\n\nWhich one ofus is frowning and complaining and unhappy?\n\nI am. Because ..\n\nAnd which one of us is happy?\n\nYou are. Because ..\n\nAnd which kind of person is happy: the oppressed or the free?\n\nThe free.\n\nSee? We are the free. You are the oppressed.\n\nThis is ndiculous. Why are we oppressed, according to your wacky perspective?",
