          "speakerAm": "ገጽ 352 (የቀጠለ)",
          "role": "prose",
          "en": "It will feel ngid at first, but rigid forms arc necessary for beginners in every ficld. Aspiring pocts should first learn to write sonnets before wnting free verse.\n\nPianists must master scales and chords and Bach's two-part Inventions. Babies need walkers. and the lame nced crutches, and sinners need “organized reli- gion.” The principles below can apply to argumentative essays of any length but especially to a medium length cssay in the neighborhood of 3-6 pages.\n\nHOW TO WRITE A LOGICAL (ARGUMENTATIVE) ESSAY I. Choose a good topic. A good topic for a logical essay has all three of the fol- lowing qualitics:\n\n(a) It is controversial, that is, argued-about, not obvious. “War is painful™is not controversial; “all wars are unjust” is. “Man is mortal” 1s not contro- versial: “man can bc madc immortal”is.",
