          "en": "B. Some rules about protocol and procedures:\n\n1.\n\nReasons must always be given when asked for. “Why?” is always a legiti- mate question.\n\n2.\n\n“Follow the argument wherever it goes.” Reason is the common master.\n\nThe two debaters are like rafts, and the argumentis like a river.\n\n3.\n\nThe river has both calm and turbulent parts, and perhaps rocks and water- falls. But the aim 1s to find the sea, not to tip your opponent's raft over.\n\n4.\n\nAlways listen before you respond, so that you respond to what was actual- ly said. In fact, no onc has the right to respond to his opponent’s argument",
