          "speakerAm": "ገጽ 369፦ Logic and theology / Logic and mathematics",
          "role": "prose",
          "en": "Logic and theology / Logic and mathematics for the existence of God, such as Aquinas's “five ways,” try to show that the ansSwcer 1s yes.\n\nBut can any sense data prove or disprove the existence of a God who by def- inition cannot be sensed? Modern empincists claim that the answer 1s no; that God's existence cannot in principle be proved.\n\nCan formal logic alone disprove atheism — i.e. is atheism logically self-con- tradictory? St. Anselm's famous “ontological argument” answers yes.\n\nDoesthe existence of evil (which by definition is the opposite of good) dis- prove an infinitely good God? The most famous argument for atheism answers yes.\n\nWhatever your answeris, it must answer the arguments of the other side.\n\nThe debate over the existence of God is not merely onc about faith, it is one about logic too. It is not just “sharing personal feelings™but a hard look at facts and arguments.",
          "am": "ይህ ክፍል በገጽ 369 ላይ የቀረበውን የሶክራታዊ ሎጂክ ዋና ሐሳብ ያካትታል። ሙሉው የእንግሊዝኛ ይዘት በትይዩ ተቀምጧል።",
          "notes": "Peter Kreeft, Socratic Logic (Ed. 3.1), Page 369."
